---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { demoData } from '../data/demo';

const tabs = [
  ['repository', 'Repository map'],
  ['impact', 'Change impact'],
  ['evidence', 'Evidence'],
  ['plan', 'Engineering plan'],
  ['safety', 'Safety loop'],
  ['reality', 'Engineering Reality']
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout title="Vericore Demo — AI-agent verification proof" description="Explore a static, reproducible Vericore 0.8.2 workflow showing how repository evidence becomes a persisted change contract and how verification catches an unexpected agent mutation.">
  <section class="intro container">
    <span class="kicker">INTERACTIVE PROOF</span>
    <h1>Follow one engineering decision from repository facts to a verified change boundary.</h1>
    <p>This is a committed demonstration artifact. It does not pretend to execute Vericore in the browser; every value is static, inspectable, and shaped around the current prepare → change → verify workflow.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="journey container" aria-label="Vericore engineering journey">
    <div class="journey-copy"><span class="kicker">THE LOOP</span><h2>One change. One persisted boundary.</h2><p>Start with repository facts, follow the impact, inspect the evidence, prepare the change, then verify the original contract after the agent edits code.</p></div>
    <ol class="journey-steps">
      <li><span>01</span><strong>Repository</strong><small>facts</small></li><li><span>02</span><strong>Impact</strong><small>blast radius</small></li><li><span>03</span><strong>Evidence</strong><small>citations</small></li><li><span>04</span><strong>Plan</strong><small>bounded work</small></li><li><span>05</span><strong>Contract</strong><small>change boundary</small></li><li><span>06</span><strong>Reality</strong><small>state binding</small></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="explorer container" aria-labelledby="explorer-title">
    <div class="explorer-head"><div><span class="kicker">SAMPLE REPOSITORY</span><h2 id="explorer-title">{demoData.repository.title}</h2></div><span class="badge">STATIC ARTIFACT</span></div>
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Demo views">
      {tabs.map(([id, label], index) => <button class:list={{ active: index === 0 }} class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected={index === 0} aria-controls={`panel-${id}`} data-tab={id}>{label}</button>)}
    </div>
    <div id="panel-repository" class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-panel="repository">
      <div class="panel-intro"><span class="step-label">01 / REPOSITORY</span><strong>Start with deterministic structure.</strong><span>Vericore maps the codebase before higher-level reasoning begins.</span></div>
      <div class="stats"><div><strong>{demoData.repository.files}</strong><span>files in sample snapshot</span></div><div><strong>{demoData.repository.relationships}</strong><span>relationships in sample snapshot</span></div><div><strong>{demoData.repository.hotspots}</strong><span>knowledge hotspots in sample snapshot</span></div></div>
      <div class="graph" aria-label="Dependency graph for the example repository"><svg class="edges" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">{demoData.repository.edges.map(([from, to]) => { const a = demoData.repository.nodes.find((node) => node.name === from)!; const b = demoData.repository.nodes.find((node) => node.name === to)!; return <line x1={a.x} y1={a.y} x2={b.x} y2={b.y} />; })}</svg>{demoData.repository.nodes.map((node) => <div class={`node ${node.kind}`} style={`left:${node.x}%;top:${node.y}%`}><span>{node.kind}</span><strong>{node.name}</strong></div>)}</div>
      <p class="caption">The numbers above are demonstration data, not a claim about this repository. Real Vericore analysis is performed by the CLI/local application.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="panel-impact" class="panel hidden" role="tabpanel" data-panel="impact" aria-hidden="true"><div class="panel-intro"><span class="step-label">02 / IMPACT</span><strong>Follow the blast radius before editing.</strong><span>Dependency-aware impact turns a changed component into an explicit set of affected areas.</span></div><div class="impact-layout"><div class="change-card"><span class="kicker">CHANGED</span><strong>{demoData.impact.changed}</strong><p>Potentially changes behaviour across the connected payment flow.</p></div><div class="affected-list"><span class="kicker">AFFECTED COMPONENTS</span>{demoData.impact.affected.map((item) => <div class="affected"><strong>{item.name}</strong><span>{item.reason}</span></div>)}</div></div><div class="notice"><strong>Risk signal</strong><span>{demoData.impact.risk}</span></div><div class="notice muted"><strong>Known uncertainty</strong><span>{demoData.impact.uncertainty}</span></div></div>
    <div id="panel-evidence" class="panel hidden" role="tabpanel" data-panel="evidence"><div class="panel-intro"><span class="step-label">03 / EVIDENCE</span><strong>Every conclusion has a bounded source.</strong><span>Evidence makes repository reasoning inspectable instead of turning a model response into an unsupported claim.</span></div><div class="evidence-list">{demoData.evidence.map((item) => <article><div class="evidence-id">{item.id}</div><div><strong>{item.finding}</strong><span>{item.source}</span></div><em>{item.confidence}</em></article>)}</div><p class="caption">The evidence view illustrates the traceability model; it is not a live query against a visitor's repository.</p></div>
    <div id="panel-plan" class="panel hidden" role="tabpanel" data-panel="plan"><div class="panel-intro"><span class="step-label">04 / PLAN</span><strong>Turn evidence into bounded work.</strong><span>The planner is read-only: it proposes affected components, risks, implementation steps, and verification criteria before changes begin.</span></div><div class="plan-list">{demoData.plan.map(([number, title, detail]) => <article><span>{number}</span><div><strong>{title}</strong><p>{detail}</p></div></article>)}</div><div class="plan-footer">Grounded planning keeps repository evidence ahead of implementation decisions.</div></div>
    <div id="panel-safety" class="panel hidden" role="tabpanel" data-panel="safety" aria-hidden="true"><div class="panel-intro"><span class="step-label">05 / CONTRACT</span><strong>Cross a persisted change boundary.</strong><span>Prepare records what was allowed to change and what must be verified later.</span></div><div class="safety-head"><div><span class="kicker">PREPARE</span><strong>{demoData.safety.prepared}</strong></div><span class="badge">PERSISTED CONTRACT</span></div><div class="contract-grid"><div><small>CONTRACT</small><strong>{demoData.safety.contract}</strong></div><div><small>FINGERPRINT</small><strong>{demoData.safety.fingerprint}</strong></div><div><small>VERIFY BOUNDARY</small><strong>Original prepared state</strong></div></div><div class="scope-grid"><div><span class="kicker">EXPECTED</span>{demoData.safety.plannedPaths.map((path) => <span class="scope-row"><strong>{path}</strong><em>allowed</em></span>)}</div><div class="scope-fail"><span class="kicker">DETECTED</span><span class="scope-row"><strong>{demoData.safety.detectedUnexpected}</strong><em>unexpected</em></span><b>✗ VERIFICATION FAIL</b></div></div><div class="verify-list"><span class="kicker">VERIFICATION CHECKS</span>{demoData.safety.verify.map((item, index) => <div><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{item}</strong></div>)}</div><div class="plan-footer">Vericore verifies the persisted Agent Change Contract instead of silently replacing it with a newly generated contract after the change.</div></div>
    <div id="panel-reality" class="panel hidden" role="tabpanel" data-panel="reality" aria-hidden="true"><div class="panel-intro"><span class="step-label">06 / REALITY</span><strong>Know which repository state the evidence belongs to.</strong><span>Engineering Reality binds analysis and context to repository state so stale evidence can be rejected.</span></div><div class="reality-hero"><span class="kicker">STATE BOUNDARY</span><strong>{demoData.reality.identity}</strong><p>{demoData.reality.stale}</p></div><div class="contract-grid"><div><small>ANALYSIS</small><strong>{demoData.reality.analysis}</strong></div><div><small>CONTEXT</small><strong>{demoData.reality.context}</strong></div><div><small>IDENTITY</small><strong>{demoData.reality.identity}</strong></div></div><div class="verify-list"><span class="kicker">BOUND COMPONENTS</span>{demoData.reality.binding.map((item, index) => <div><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{item}</strong></div>)}</div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="container note"><span class="kicker">WHY STATIC?</span><h2>Reproducible proof beats a fake live demo.</h2><p>GitHub Pages hosts static assets. This explorer intentionally uses committed sample artifacts so visitors can inspect the verification workflow without sending repository data to a hidden backend.</p><a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore">Inspect the real implementation ↗</a></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  const tabs = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-tab]');
  const panels = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-panel]');
  tabs.forEach((tab) => tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const id = tab.dataset.tab;
    tabs.forEach((item) => { const selected = item === tab; item.classList.toggle('active', selected); item.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected)); });
    panels.forEach((panel) => { const active = panel.dataset.panel === id; panel.classList.toggle('hidden', !active); panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', String(!active)); });
  }));
</script>
<style>
  .intro{padding:100px 0 42px;max-width:920px}.kicker{color:var(--accent);font:600 .72rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em}.intro h1{max-width:880px;margin:14px 0;font-size:clamp(2.8rem,7vw,5.8rem);line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.06em}.intro p,.note p{max-width:720px;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem}.journey{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.5fr;gap:34px;align-items:center;padding:20px 0 54px}.journey-copy h2{margin:8px 0;font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3vw,2.5rem);letter-spacing:-.04em}.journey-copy p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.journey-steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:8px;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none}.journey-steps li{padding:15px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--panel)}.journey-steps span,.journey-steps small{display:block;color:var(--accent);font:.62rem ui-monospace,monospace}.journey-steps strong{display:block;margin:8px 0 2px;font-size:.82rem}.journey-steps small{color:var(--muted)}.explorer{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--panel)}.explorer-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:22px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.explorer-head h2{margin:6px 0 0;font-size:1.2rem}.badge{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:6px 9px;color:var(--muted);font:.65rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.tabs{display:flex;overflow-x:auto;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.tab{appearance:none;border:0;border-right:1px solid var(--line);background:transparent;color:var(--muted);padding:14px 18px;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;font:600 .78rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace}.tab.active{color:var(--text);background:var(--panel-2);box-shadow:inset 0 -2px var(--accent)}.panel{padding:22px;min-height:430px}.hidden{display:none}.panel-intro{display:grid;gap:5px;margin-bottom:20px;max-width:760px}.panel-intro .step-label{color:var(--accent);font:600 .65rem ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em}.panel-intro strong{font-size:1.15rem}.panel-intro>span:last-child{color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.6}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:8px;margin-bottom:14px}.stats div{padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:8px}.stats strong{display:block;font-size:1.45rem;letter-spacing:-.04em}.stats span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem}.graph{position:relative;min-height:380px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background-image:linear-gradient(rgb(255 255 255 / 3%) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(255 255 255 / 3%) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:36px 36px}.edges{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%}.edges line{stroke:#334155;stroke-width:.35;stroke-dasharray:1.5 1}.node{position:absolute;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);min-width:130px;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:#0b1119;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 25%)}.node span{display:block;color:var(--accent);font:.58rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;text-transform:uppercase}.node strong{display:block;margin-top:3px;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap}.node.repository{border-color:#374151}.node.test{border-style:dashed}.impact-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.5fr;gap:12px}.change-card,.affected-list,.notice,.contract-grid>div,.reality-hero{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;padding:22px;background:var(--panel-2)}.change-card strong{display:block;margin-top:18px;font-size:1.4rem}.change-card p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem}.affected-list>.kicker{display:block;margin-bottom:10px}.affected{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.affected span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}.notice{margin-top:12px;display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:baseline}.notice strong{white-space:nowrap}.notice span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}.notice.muted{opacity:.85}.evidence-list,.plan-list{display:grid;gap:8px}.evidence-list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:60px 1fr auto;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--panel-2)}.evidence-id{color:var(--accent);font:600 .78rem ui-monospace,monospace}.evidence-list strong,.evidence-list span{display:block}.evidence-list span{color:var(--muted);font:.72rem ui-monospace,monospace;margin-top:4px}.evidence-list em{color:var(--success);font:.68rem ui-monospace,monospace}.caption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}.plan-list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.plan-list article>span{color:var(--accent);font:.78rem ui-monospace,monospace}.plan-list p{margin:4px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}.plan-footer{margin-top:18px;padding:16px;border-left:2px solid var(--accent);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem}.safety-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;gap:20px;padding-bottom:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.safety-head strong{display:block;margin-top:8px;font-size:1.4rem}.contract-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:8px;margin-top:12px}.contract-grid small{display:block;color:var(--muted);font:.65rem ui-monospace,monospace}.contract-grid strong{display:block;margin-top:8px;font-size:.8rem}.scope-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:16px}.scope-grid>div{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;padding:18px;background:var(--panel-2)}.scope-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.8rem}.scope-row em{font-style:normal;color:var(--success);font:.68rem ui-monospace,monospace;text-transform:uppercase}.scope-fail .scope-row em{color:var(--danger,#ff6b7a)}.scope-fail b{display:block;margin-top:14px;color:var(--danger,#ff6b7a);font:.72rem ui-monospace,monospace}.verify-list{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:24px}.verify-list>.kicker{margin-bottom:8px}.verify-list>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:40px 1fr;gap:12px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.verify-list>div span{color:var(--accent);font:600 .75rem ui-monospace,monospace}.verify-list>div strong{font-size:.82rem}.reality-hero strong{display:block;margin:12px 0 4px;font-size:1.35rem}.reality-hero p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65}.note{padding:110px 0 10px}.note h2{margin:10px 0;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.3rem);letter-spacing:-.04em}.note a{display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;color:var(--accent);text-underline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:900px){.journey{grid-template-columns:1fr}.journey-steps{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}@media(max-width:700px){.intro{padding-top:70px}.panel{min-height:0}.stats,.impact-layout,.contract-grid,.scope-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.graph{min-height:440px}.node{min-width:110px}.evidence-list article{grid-template-columns:48px 1fr}.evidence-list em{grid-column:2}.notice,.safety-head{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:6px}.journey-steps{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.journey{padding-bottom:34px}}@media(max-width:430px){.journey-steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}.journey-steps li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:34px 1fr;align-items:center}.journey-steps span{grid-row:1 / span 2}.journey-steps small{grid-column:2}.journey-steps strong{margin:0}}
</style>
